sections.text:
All pet owners and handlers within the City of Davao shall strictly observe the following obligations:

(a) Maintain their dogs within a securely fenced yard, enclosure, or residential compound so as to prevent the animal from escaping onto public streets or neighboring properties;

(b) Keep their dogs on a secure leash not exceeding two (2) meters in length whenever walking or exercising the animal along public sidewalks, parks, coastal roads, or greenways, and place a humane basket muzzle on dogs with a documented history of aggression;

(c) Immediately collect, bag, and properly dispose of any fecal matter deposited by their pet on any public street, sidewalk, park, or neighbor's property into designated sanitary waste receptacles;

(d) Provide their animals with adequate daily nutrition, clean potable water, ventilated shelter protected from extreme heat and rain, and prompt veterinary care when ill or injured;

(e) Refrain from abandoning any sick, aged, or unwanted domestic animal on public streets, vacant lots, or watershed areas.

Any person, pet owner, commercial kennel operator, or corporate officer who violates any provision of this Ordinance shall, upon conviction, be punished in accordance with the following graduated penalty schedule:

(a) First Offense: A fine of Twenty-Five Thousand Pesos (Php 25,000.00) and mandatory community service of forty (40) hours;

(b) Second Offense: A fine of Thirty-Five Thousand Pesos (Php 35,000.00) or imprisonment for a period of one (1) year and six (6) months;

(c) Third and Subsequent Offenses: A fine of Fifty Thousand Pesos (Php 50,000.00) and imprisonment for a fixed term of three (3) years, plus permanent revocation of the Mayor's Business Permit in the case of commercial kennels, pet shops, or veterinary establishments.
